{"requirements":[{"id":"nginx-http-6700","requirement":"On node1, Nginx must serve a successful HTTP response at `/` over TCP port 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks showed Nginx active and listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 6700, with `http://10.100.225.10:6700/` returning HTTP 200 and the expected body both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc6542d621a14bf5","cmd-dd302b2749b34c78","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All explicit state-changing commands had clear roles: installing Nginx, adding its port-6700 configuration, configuring SELinux and firewalld, enabling the service, and performing the mandatory restart. Restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered HTTP/service state, independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations. Package health remained intact, no failed services or abandoned temporary artifacts were observed. One low-severity retained unnecessary side effect remains: activating the packaged default configuration also left Nginx listening on port 80, although the executor only added a firewall rule for port 6700. This extra listener arose from the package installation and service activation and was not reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-90de3311fac64102","cmd-1e2dfaa79c554f9d","cmd-006593ca86ec49e7","cmd-a04bd14a4bad4707","cmd-456965ed4de44855","cmd-c123c2be65b447af","cmd-0084e1f8dd5649db","cmd-c125403f3bea4232","cmd-dd302b2749b34c78","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task is satisfied. Nginx returned HTTP 200 at `/` on TCP port 6700 and remained healthy after a verified node restart. Evidence quality is strong and coherent; hygiene is reduced slightly because the unused packaged port-80 listener remained active.","limitations":["The HTTP probes were executed from node1 against its own managed IP rather than from an independent remote client (cmd-cc6542d621a14bf5, cmd-dd302b2749b34c78)."]}
